  {"i":302,"keep":[],"n":"'Single/unmarried' is a minor usage. 一人 is taught under people/numbers, not the family unit."},
  {"i":304,"keep":[1],"n":"Being absent or taking a day off (会社を休む, 学校を休む) is a core N5 sense and is taught in the work and school units."},
  {"i":372,"keep":[],"n":"大 alone as 'university' is a clipped form found in compounds like 東大. Learners meet the word 大学 instead."},
  {"i":396,"keep":[2],"n":"'Now, at present' (ただいま電話に出られません) is common and belongs in the time unit. 'Just now' and 'right away' are rarer for learners."},
  {"i":399,"keep":[],"n":"'Metal' for かね is archaic or literary. Learners meet 金 (かね) only as money."},
  {"i":411,"keep":[3,4],"n":"Degree and vague adverb uses (どうもおかしい, どうも分からない) are common at N4-N3 and fit the function unit."},
  {"i":412,"keep":[4],"n":"'Awkward or problematic' (それはまずい) is very common and is a general quality. The 'uh-oh' interjection is not an emotion topic."},
  {"i":423,"keep":[],"n":"'Heap or pile' (山ほど) is figurative or quantity-like. A teacher would not teach 山 in the numbers unit."},
  {"i":449,"keep":[1],"n":"Degrees of temperature (今日は30度) are common, so the weather topic is justified for sense 1."}
